<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal must join EU currency in first group-PM.</title>
<headline>Portugal must join EU currency in first group-PM.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prime Minister Antonio Guterres said it was vital that Portugal was among the first group of countries to join a single European currency.</p>
<p>&quot;It is essential that Portugal should be one of the founder countries of the single currency as this (single currency) is one of the decisions that will mould the future of Europe,&quot; Guterres told a lunch organised by the Portuguese-Arab Chamber of Commerce.</p>
<p>The Socialist government is trying to meet strict economic targets to join a single European currency by the end of the century.</p>
<p>Earlier on Wednesday, Bank of Spain governor Luis Angel Rojo said in Madrid that Spain must be in the first phase of monetary union too. He said it would be &quot;a clear mistake for Spain not be included in EMU&quot;.</p>
<p>-- David Brough, Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
